planningNotes.risks:
VS Code differs from JetBrains in three ways, which this row documents only by omission and does not fix:
- runtimeProfile returns 'protected' for a project pinned in this session before it reads project.json, so a same-session verified-local re-declaration records nothing (JetBrains got that in task-6d5d3db2);
- an Allow answered later persists legacy whatever the declaration says by then;
- a store root that cannot be written leaves no record, so after a restart a legacy declaration runs legacy with no prompt (the Accepted Windows costs bullet covers the share case).
The dotted setting ids moe.daemon.host/port live in moe-vscode/package.json, not in src, and DoD 1 limits names to moe-vscode/src, so write them as the `moe` settings `daemon.host` and `daemon.port`.
The ARCHITECTURE line numbers shift as rows land: anchor on the bullet text, not the line.
